# grappa — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env and fill in the prod-required block before
# `scripts/deploy.sh`. Dev (`docker compose up` with no profile) leaves
# the prod block unset and uses fixed dev values from config/dev.exs.

# Match host UID/GID so bind-mounted source files are owned correctly.
CONTAINER_UID=1000
CONTAINER_GID=1000

# Mix environment switch. `dev` for local hacking, `prod` for the
# deploy.sh stack. Phoenix expects an atom without the leading colon
# when read from env vars (just `prod`).
#
# NOTE: compose interpolates this into BOTH `MIX_ENV` and `DATABASE_PATH`
# (`grappa_${MIX_ENV:-dev}.db`), so the value below picks which database
# every container and oneshot opens. `scripts/deploy.sh` exports
# `MIX_ENV=prod` for its own invocations and the shell wins over this
# file (#1377 D-S3) — but a hand-driven `docker compose --profile prod
# …` on a prod box inherits exactly what is written here. Set it to
# `prod` on any box that is not a dev laptop.
MIX_ENV=dev

# Host port publish for the grappa container. #485 dropped the in-stack
# nginx, so grappa is the LAN-facing service now. Defaults to loopback-only
# (`127.0.0.1:4000`): the bouncer is unreachable from the LAN unless you
# override this OR front it with your own TLS reverse proxy
# (infra/nginx-tls-frontend.example.conf). Override examples:
#   GRAPPA_PUBLISH=192.168.53.12:4000   # bind to a LAN/VLAN IP
#   GRAPPA_PUBLISH=0.0.0.0:4000          # all interfaces (firewall it!)
#   GRAPPA_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:14000       # alternate localhost port
# compose.override.yaml.example shows the canonical "bind to LAN IP" +
# PHX_HOST + EXTRA_CHECK_ORIGINS triple — prefer the override file for that
# shape (avoids shell-quoting).
GRAPPA_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:4000

# Canonical WebAuthn origin. Usually inferred from PHX_HOST; useful when
# development UI runs on a separate origin (for example http://localhost:5173).
# GRAPPA_PASSKEY_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# DEPRECATED (#485) — NGINX_PUBLISH published the removed nginx container
# and is no longer read by compose.yaml. `infra/docker/deploy.sh update`
# rewrites a legacy .env for you (GRAPPA_PUBLISH = NGINX_PUBLISH minus the
# container-side :80). Kept documented for one release so an operator who
# still carries it recognises it; set GRAPPA_PUBLISH instead.
# NGINX_PUBLISH=3000:80

# ─── Required for prod (`--profile prod` deploys) ─────────────────────────────
# Public hostname the bouncer is reached at (e.g. grappa.example.org) —
# via your own TLS front door, or directly. NO default — config/runtime.exs
# RAISES at boot if
# this is unset/empty in prod, so a copied-but-unedited file fails LOUDLY
# instead of silently minting dead upload links + rejecting every
# WebSocket handshake (Origin mismatch). Leave blank for local dev
# (stays localhost).
PHX_HOST=

# Generate with:  scripts/mix.sh phx.gen.secret
SECRET_KEY_BASE=

# Plug.Session signing salt — Phoenix recommends 32+ random bytes.
# Generate with:  scripts/mix.sh phx.gen.secret 32
SECRET_SIGNING_SALT=

# Cloak vault key — base64-encoded 32 bytes. Encrypts at-rest upstream
# credentials (sasl_password etc.) in the sqlite DB.
# Generate ONCE per deployment with:
#   scripts/mix.sh grappa.gen_encryption_key
# Back this up separately! Losing the key = losing all stored credentials.
GRAPPA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# VAPID keypair — push notifications cluster B2 (2026-05-14).
# Required for Web Push delivery (RFC 8292).
# Generate ONCE per deployment with:
#   scripts/mix.sh grappa.gen_vapid
# Bootstrap raises at boot if either is missing. Losing the PRIVATE
# key invalidates every existing browser push subscription — rotation
# forces every user to re-toggle the master switch in cic settings.
# Operators typically pin these in compose.override.yaml's grappa
# environment block instead of .env (see compose.override.yaml.example).
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional — `sub` claim in the VAPID JWT, surfaced to vendor push
# services so they can contact the operator about delivery issues.
# Defaults to mailto:admin@example.org if unset.
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.org

# Erlang distribution cookie. Gates `bin/grappa remote-shell` access
# (T cluster T-2, 2026-05-16). The dev default
# `grappa-dev-cookie-do-not-use-in-prod` is hardcoded in compose.yaml
# so `docker compose up` works clone-and-go; runtime.exs HARD-CRASHES
# at boot in MIX_ENV=prod when this is unset OR equals the dev sentinel.
# Generate a real value with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Threat model: anyone with `docker exec` privilege can `printenv` the
# cookie inside the container, AND any container attached to the
# `grappa_internal` bridge (today: the cicchetto-build oneshot)
# with Erlang installed could `:net_adm.ping(:grappa@grappa)` if it
# knew the cookie. Distribution port is never published to the host —
# the cookie is a same-host operator gate (sname-collision-prevention
# + "you meant to do this") not a network boundary. Rotation requires
# a COLD deploy and invalidates all live admin remsh sessions.
# Leave commented in dev (compose.yaml default applies); MUST be set
# for prod deploys.
# RELEASE_COOKIE=

# ─── Optional in prod (sensible defaults applied) ─────────────────────────────
# Ecto pool size. Defaults to 10. Sqlite is single-writer; raising pool size
# helps read concurrency, not write throughput.
POOL_SIZE=10

# Phoenix HTTP listener port. Defaults to 4000.
PORT=4000

# UX-6-B1 (2026-05-20): embedded image uploader storage directory.
# Defaults to `runtime/uploads` (sibling of the sqlite DB; covered by
# the existing `./runtime:/app/runtime` bind-mount). Override only if
# disk-policy requires a separate volume. Cap admin-tunes per-file +
# global-disk ceilings live in `server_settings` table (admin REST).
UPLOADS_STORAGE_ROOT=runtime/uploads

# #399: directory holding the built cicchetto SPA (index.html + assets/
# + backgrounds/ + fonts/ + service-worker.js + manifest). The embedded
# Phoenix web server serves it via Plug.Static + a SPA history-mode
# fallback + the security-header plug, so a plain service start yields a
# fully working instance — #485 dropped the nginx container and grappa
# self-serves the frontend. Defaults to `runtime/cicchetto-dist` (the dir
# every cic build writes). A packaged install points this at its data dir.
CIC_DIST_ROOT=runtime/cicchetto-dist

# NOTE (#228, 2026-07-14): the outbound v6 source-address pool is no
# longer an env var. GRAPPA_OUTBOUND_V6_POOL was REMOVED — the rotation
# pool is now DB-driven (the `in_pool` vhosts, curated in the admin
# panel → Vhosts tab). See docs/OPERATIONS.md "Vhost (source-bind)
# selection". Nothing to set here.

# Logger level: :debug | :info | :notice | :warning | :error. Prod default :info.
# Read via String.to_existing_atom/1 — must be a known Logger level atom.
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Extra origins accepted by the WebSocket `check_origin` gate alongside
# PHX_HOST, AND — with PHX_HOST — the source of the deployment's HTTP
# host-alias set (#324). Comma-separated, full origin form
# (https://host, no trailing slash). Prod should pin to PHX_HOST only;
# this is an escape-hatch for raw-IP / secondary-vhost reach (LAN
# testing, a second public hostname). Empty / unset = no extras.
# EXTRA_CHECK_ORIGINS=https://192.168.53.12:3000,https://irc.example.org

# BEAM resource caps (see bin/start.sh). Unset → defaults applied
# (GRAPPA_MAX_USERS=100, GRAPPA_DIRTY_SCHEDULERS=$(nproc)).
# GRAPPA_MAX_USERS=100
# GRAPPA_DIRTY_SCHEDULERS=

# #543 — outbound source-alias substrate: jail | linux | docker. Selects the
# static-mapping (mode 2) source-binding adapter. Unset/unknown → docker
# (Disabled → mode 2 refuses to arm). Set jail on the FreeBSD bastille (sudo
# ifconfig lo0 wrapper) or linux on a native host (AnyIP route +
# net.ipv6.ip_nonlocal_bind=1). Docker cannot provide either — leave unset.
# GRAPPA_SUBSTRATE=docker

# ─── cicchetto bundle build (compose-only, `--profile prod`) ──────────────────
# #1037: both are read by compose.yaml ALONE — neither reaches config/runtime.exs
# or bin/start.sh, so neither is an app var. Every deploy wrapper already sets
# them; documented for the operator who drives `docker compose --profile prod
# run --rm cicchetto-build` by hand.
#
# GRAPPA_VERSION is the `cicchetto-build` `environment:` entry vite bakes into
# `<meta name="cicchetto-version">` (#538/#652). Compose forwards it as EMPTY
# when unset and vite then REFUSES to build, rather than ship an unversioned
# bundle — the container mounts only ./cicchetto, so it cannot read the
# repo-root VERSION itself. The wrappers derive it per launch via
# infra/packaging/version.sh. Set it to stamp a bundle with something other
# than the checkout's VERSION.
# GRAPPA_VERSION=
#
# CIC_BUILD_OUT is the host side of that service's `volumes:` mount — where the
# built SPA lands. Defaults to the directory the BEAM serves (CIC_DIST_ROOT
# above). vite EMPTIES its out dir before writing, so building straight into
# the served directory serves an empty SPA for the whole build (#1020): the
# wrappers point this at a staging sibling and rename it into place. Override
# with the same staging-then-rename discipline.
# CIC_BUILD_OUT=./runtime/cicchetto-dist

# ─── T31 admission captcha (optional — leave unset for Disabled provider) ─────
# config/runtime.exs reads these env vars to populate :grappa, :admission
# config (provider, secret, public site key). Provider absent / unknown =
# Disabled (boots clean, never emits captcha_required at the boundary).
# Non-Disabled providers HARD-CRASH at boot if secret or site_key is
# missing/blank (Grappa.Admission.Config.boot/0 invariant).
#
# When enabling, also ensure the CSP allowlist in
# GrappaWeb.Plugs.SecurityHeaders covers the provider host (#485 moved the
# CSP off nginx into the app). Drift breaks deploy in a way only
# real-browser e2e catches (per CP11 S22 deploy-time bug post-mortem).
#
# `GRAPPA_CAPTCHA_SITE_KEY` is the public widget identifier issued by
# the captcha provider for your domain — embedded in the served HTML
# and safe to publish. Replace the placeholder below with your own.
# GRAPPA_CAPTCHA_PROVIDER=turnstile  # or hcaptcha; absent = disabled
# GRAPPA_CAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=0xYOUR_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY_HERE
# GRAPPA_CAPTCHA_SECRET=

# ─── #1027 shottino --ircd bridge (opt-in: `docker compose --profile ircd up`) ─
# A real IRC server on a port, so irssi/weechat/hexchat/goguma reach grappa
# without speaking its REST + Channels protocol. Nothing below is read unless
# the `ircd` profile is active.
#
# ONE SERVICE PER USER, not per network: a downstream client names the network
# it wants in `PASS <network>:<password>`, and that is stored per connection —
# so three networks are three `/connect`s to this ONE port. A second grappa
# ACCOUNT is what needs a second service on a second port.
#
# SHOTTINO_USER is the grappa username the bridge logs in as. Unset, the login
# fails and `restart: unless-stopped` turns that into a restart loop — check
# this first when the bridge will not stay up.
# SHOTTINO_USER=you
#
# SHOTTINO_PASSWORD is that login's password. It is an env var and not an
# argument on purpose: headless there is no terminal to prompt, and the
# command line shows it to every user on the host via `ps` for as long as the
# bridge runs — which for a bridge is permanently.
# SHOTTINO_PASSWORD=
#
# SHOTTINO_IRCD_PASS is what DOWNSTREAM clients must send (`PASS
# <network>:<this>`). MANDATORY here: a published port is off-loopback from
# the bridge's point of view, and off loopback shottino refuses to listen
# without it — the bridge hands over the whole IRC session, every channel,
# every DM, and the ability to speak as you.
# SHOTTINO_IRCD_PASS=
#
# Where the bridge is published on the HOST. Loopback by default, same
# convention as GRAPPA_PUBLISH. Widen it and you are exposing that session to
# whoever can reach the address.
# SHOTTINO_IRCD_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:6667
#
# Which grappa the bridge talks to. In-stack over grappa_internal by default;
# point it at a public https:// URL to bridge somebody else's instance.
# SHOTTINO_GRAPPA_URL=http://grappa:4000
